BEHAVIOR array-push

DESCRIPTION
  Appends value to the array if there is room (len < cap), incrementing len.
  status = 1 if appended, 0 if the array was full (value dropped). Operates on
  the caller-owned buffer from array-init.

CONTRACT
  INPUT arr bytes 65536
  INPUT value int 8
  OUTPUT status int 8
  GUARANTEES writes_output

HASH c9c2e445

IMPLEMENTATION
  len = LOAD arr 8 0
  cap = LOAD arr 8 8
  full = IGE len cap 8
  BRANCH full isfull dopush
  LABEL dopush
    v = LOAD value 8
    e = IMUL len 8 8
    off = IADD e 16 8
    STORE arr v 8 off
    nl = IADD len 1 8
    STORE arr nl 8 0
    STORE status 1 8
    JUMP pdone
  LABEL isfull
    STORE status 0 8
  LABEL pdone
END
